      <ul>
        <li><strong>Total Tasks Completed</strong> across all team members</li>
        <li><strong>AI Utilization %</strong> — how many are actively working right now</li>
        <li><strong>Human Hours Saved</strong> — real ROI, calculated daily</li>
        <li><strong>API Spend</strong> — exactly what your AI team costs to run</li>
        <li><strong>Team Health Score</strong> — composite 0-100 across reliability, throughput, and efficiency</li>
        <li><strong>Performance Leaderboard</strong> — which team member is crushing it today</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p>Every action is logged. Every cost is visible. Every team member is accountable. If something breaks, you don't find out three days later when a client complains — you see a red dot and an alert in your queue within seconds.</p>

    <h2>But What If AI Makes a Mistake?</h2>

    <p>Fair question. Trust is earned.</p>

    <p>This isn't autopilot — it's co-pilot. AI pre-fills, humans approve. You control the safety level. Want AI to send routine confirmations automatically? Fine. Want human approval for anything over $500? Also fine.</p>

    <p>AI does the tedious work — data extraction, first drafts, status updates — but you maintain final approval on anything that matters. It's not about replacing judgment. It's about eliminating the drudgery that buries your judgment under busywork.</p>

    <h2>How Fast Can This Happen?</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Client communication assistant:</strong> 1-2 weeks</li>
      <li><strong>Workflow automation:</strong> 2-3 weeks</li>
      <li><strong>Full AI department:</strong> 4-6 weeks</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Start with a pilot of 10-20 transactions to prove ROI. We don't do six-month implementations. We start small, prove value, then scale.</p>

    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>What if our team resists AI?</strong></summary>
      <p>Show them the time savings, not the technology. When someone realizes AI can eliminate their least favorite task, resistance turns into advocacy. We've never had pushback after the first week of results.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>How is this different from hiring another employee?</strong></summary>
      <p>An employee costs $50-80K annually plus benefits. AI costs a fraction of that, works 24/7, never gets sick, and scales instantly. Plus you can see exactly what it's doing every hour of every day.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>What about mistakes?</strong></summary>
      <p>Human oversight is built into every workflow. Critical decisions require approval. Routine tasks run automatically. You set the boundaries based on your risk tolerance.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>How long until we see results?</strong></summary>
      <p>You'll see value in the first week. Full ROI typically becomes obvious within 30 days as the system learns your processes and gains your team's trust.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>Can we start small?</strong></summary>
      <p>Absolutely. Most clients start with one specific workflow — usually their biggest time sink. We prove the concept, then expand systematically based on ROI.</p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary><strong>What does it cost?</strong></summary>
      <p>A fraction of hiring even one employee. We'll build a custom quote based on your specific workflows, but most small businesses save money from month one.</p>
    </details>

